                        "form": "буду/будешь… эксгуми́ровать"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "50c2bb75-498b-3a9a-90a9-b9aa579d118d",
                        "entry_id": "a88b3a32-4f27-3a4b-8070-a1bb3e30348a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн., юр., мед. осуществлять (осуществить) эксгумацию, то есть извлекать (извлечь) труп из места захоронения для судебно-медицинской, криминалистической экспертизы, патологоанатомического исследования или перезахоронения в другом месте"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "71d2713d-23cf-4164-85e9-04abf433d072",
                                "sense_id": "50c2bb75-498b-3a9a-90a9-b9aa579d118d",
                                "text": "Однако представители «Народного союза Германии» говорят, что, поскольку кладбище уже существует, вновь эксгумировать останки немецких солдат нецелесообразно."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ab2e1ba-29ac-46b9-828b-a4b191574d55",
                                "sense_id": "50c2bb75-498b-3a9a-90a9-b9aa579d118d",
                                "text": "Садись и пиши: «Прошу эксгумировать тело Семы Кабанчика»."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "730b7c59-5c7e-47c8-98eb-1e9cf45b2b72",
                        "source_entry_id": "a88b3a32-4f27-3a4b-8070-a1bb3e30348a",
                        "source_sense_id": "50c2bb75-498b-3a9a-90a9-b9aa579d118d",
                        "target_lang_word": "exhume",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exhume",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0aeaeec5-39dc-320f-8cc5-dce696f626fa",
                                        "entry_id": "d7004440-0c16-3870-b52b-fdede7acc488",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dig out of the ground; to take out of a place of burial; to disinter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "859d452e-e1df-4de1-9a6d-899a3e586b13",
                                                "sense_id": "0aeaeec5-39dc-320f-8cc5-dce696f626fa",
                                                "text": "The archeologist exhumed artifacts from the ground with a shovel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "392a1632-b4ad-41f3-a9cc-9c2d4c73d8be",
                                                "sense_id": "0aeaeec5-39dc-320f-8cc5-dce696f626fa",
                                                "text": "Not so long ago a Scotsman is reported to have exhumed the body of his daughter and burnt her heart, as he thought she was devitalising her remaining brother and sister and making them ill."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72935d89-f2a2-3435-b4c9-cf6982c2aa60",
                                        "entry_id": "d7004440-0c16-3870-b52b-fdede7acc488",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To uncover; to bring to light."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "906135b6-de3b-415f-881c-282757b3b198",
                                                "sense_id": "72935d89-f2a2-3435-b4c9-cf6982c2aa60",
                                                "text": "Memorial was permeated by a sense of mission, a moral imperative to exhume the truth and display it to the eyes of its compatriots, whatever feelings of shame, outrage, denial, or shock might ensue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f077582f-a489-449b-bc1a-4a6fac40c096",
                        "source_entry_id": "a88b3a32-4f27-3a4b-8070-a1bb3e30348a",
                        "source_sense_id": "50c2bb75-498b-3a9a-90a9-b9aa579d118d",
                        "target_lang_word": "disinter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disinter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4af9aae-9ad9-33e4-8e08-5283d7676acf",
                                        "entry_id": "3636a4ad-d23b-354a-9728-fa23ec09b5c0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take out of the grave or tomb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b1546ed-2ee3-3393-be92-9a4960b79b70",
                                        "entry_id": "3636a4ad-d23b-354a-9728-fa23ec09b5c0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bring out, as from a grave or hiding place; to bring from obscurity into view."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29d3b1bf-7309-4fec-9446-53f3eac9dc35",
                                                "sense_id": "4b1546ed-2ee3-3393-be92-9a4960b79b70",
                                                "text": "Why disinter dead faith from mouldering hidden?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a4f9a19-04c4-4fb9-8716-4fa5b64ad3c8",
                                                "sense_id": "4b1546ed-2ee3-3393-be92-9a4960b79b70",
                                                "text": "At this moment, however, the rooms bore every mark of having been recently and hurriedly ransacked; clothes lay about the floor, with their pockets inside out; lock-fast drawers stood open; and on the hearth there lay a pile of grey ashes, as though many papers had been burned. From these embers the inspector disinterred the butt end of a green cheque book, which had resisted the action of the fire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "847fab8e-61e3-4931-b03e-5765ea86e550",
                                                "sense_id": "4b1546ed-2ee3-3393-be92-9a4960b79b70",
                                                "text": "In his lectures he is equally wide-ranging and allusive, making strange links and analogies between apparently unrelated texts and ideas, and disinterring etymologies which writers cannot have been aware of."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a503c8af-9c95-4256-b217-bbc7dbe9ede6",
                        "source_entry_id": "a88b3a32-4f27-3a4b-8070-a1bb3e30348a",
                        "source_sense_id": "50c2bb75-498b-3a9a-90a9-b9aa579d118d",
